STUDENT PAIR WORKFLOW & METHODOLOGY NOTES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Before starting Strategy 1 (FR), we verified that the production code under
modules/oap/ is completely frozen at commit 4e4cb54 and no changes would be
made to production code. We launched Ollama locally and initialized a completely
fresh conversation session so no previous context or code was visible to the model.

In accordance with Section 7 of the assignment instructions, we followed a two-phase
generation process:
1. First, we provided ONLY the specification (Problem Statement + CFR/AFR). The AI
   was strictly forbidden from seeing or inferring from implementation code.
2. We inspected and froze the resulting design JSON (FR_DESIGN.json).
3. Only after the design was frozen did we supply the implementation codebase and
   request executable pytest test methods.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 1: TEST DESIGN GENERATION (FROM SPECIFICATION ONLY)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[Pair Input - Prompt A to Qwen2.5-Coder 1.5B]:
"You are designing automated specification-based tests for the Other Academic Procedures (OAP) Fusion ERP module.
Source of truth: Use ONLY the supplied Problem Statement and CFR/AFR Requirements Specification.
Do NOT inspect implementation code.
Do NOT infer behavior from implementation.
Do NOT introduce behavior unsupported by the supplied specification.
Generate the minimum non-redundant set of test cases needed to satisfy the strategy-specific adequacy rule in Section 7. Do not stop at an arbitrary number, do not omit an explicit test obligation to reduce the test count, and do not invent unsupported behavior. Prefer observable behavior that can subsequently be automated using pytest/pytest-django.

For every test case output exactly these fields:
- test_id
- source_id
- purpose
- preconditions
- action_or_input
- expected_result
- test_type

Output ONLY a valid JSON array. Do not provide explanation or additional prose.

Strategy-specific instruction for FR:
Cover every testable CFR/AFR with at least one test. Add a separate negative/boundary/validation/authorization case only where the requirement explicitly defines such a condition or outcome."

[Model Output Summary]:
The model processed the OAP requirements and generated 33 structured test case
objects covering requirements AFR-OAP-009 through AFR-OAP-038 (including student
leave requests, bonafide certificates, branch change applications, degree certificates,
and thesis archiving).

[Pair Verification & Freezing]:
We reviewed all 33 test items, validated that each CFR/AFR was covered by at least
one test case, confirmed that test IDs follow TC-FR-001 to TC-FR-033, and verified
valid JSON formatting. We saved and permanently froze this artifact to:
`a8_design/FR_DESIGN.json`.

